<title>BELGIUM: EU agrees new aid scheme for hop producers.</title>
<headline>EU agrees new aid scheme for hop producers.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers agreed by majority vote a simplified aid system for hop producers, EU officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Britain voted against the new flat-rate aid of 480 Ecus per hectare over five years to replace annual payments for different varieties.</p>
<p>Germany, Austria, Spain and Belgium had called for aid of over 500 Ecus per ha, whereas the European Commission had initially proposed 450.</p>
<p>Up to 20 percent of the aid can be used for special measures, including conversion of production to more marketable varieties.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
